![The Gleam Gathering logo, a stylised pair of pink letter Gs](/images/gleam-gathering.svg){.right}

Earlier this year we had a fantastic time at the first ever 100% Gleam conference. 

Gleam Gathering was a blast and it was incredible to see so many Gleamlins in
one place. There were talks from community members and Gleam core team members,
plenty of interesting conversations about Gleam, other tech and just life in
general. And all the side fun like bouldering, pizza and arcade games.

If you couldn't make it to Bristol, [all the 2026 talks have been released](https://www.youtube.com/@GleamGathering),
so you can see for yourself what the event was all about.

Now many of us are already preparing for Gleam Gathering 2027.

[Tickets are already available](https://gleamgathering.com/#register) and the
call for talks is open. If you've been working on something interesting with
Gleam, learned something worth sharing, built a library or tool, or simply have
a topic you think other Gleamlins would enjoy hearing about, make sure to 
[send your proposal!](https://gleamgathering.com/#call-for-talks)!

See you there!
